WEBVTT

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:03.255
From demonstrations, to concepts, to action.

00:00:03.255 --> 00:00:04.373
This is UniPred.

00:00:04.933 --> 00:00:09.193
An LLM agent proposes a concept, and how actions should change it.

00:00:09.753 --> 00:00:14.593
Human demonstrations connect that proposal to what the robot actually sees.

00:00:15.153 --> 00:00:19.149
The proposal becomes supervision for a visual classifier.

00:00:19.149 --> 00:00:25.179
Learning and validation feedback return to the agent, which revises its next proposal.

00:00:25.179 --> 00:00:27.493
Propose, learn, evaluate, revise.

00:00:28.053 --> 00:00:32.671
The result is a set of learned predicates: concepts grounded in observation.

00:00:33.231 --> 00:00:37.221
Together, their truth values describe a symbolic state of the world.

00:00:37.781 --> 00:00:43.647
A planner searches between these states, using learned action preconditions and effects, to reach a goal.

00:00:44.207 --> 00:00:49.775
Now the robot follows the plan: store the toys, grasp the towel, and wipe the table.

00:00:49.775 --> 00:00:54.083
After each action, it observes again, and can replan when needed.
